{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Presenting the Product", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Q & A", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 14, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about people's interests and backgrounds using a wider range of language.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing Advice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are many different ways to make recommendations and express advice. The modal verbs 'had better', 'ought to' and 'might' are most commonly used to make recommendations. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Had better</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol type=\"a\"><li>Form: subject + had better + bare infinitive (verb without 'to')</li><li>Meaning: \u201chad better\u201d is very similar in meaning to should but it is stronger because it implies a negative consequence if the advice is not followed. </li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ought to</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol type=\"a\"><li>Form: subject + ought to + bare infinitive (verb without 'to')</li><li>Meaning: \u201cought to\u201d is used for saying what you think is the right thing to do. </li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Might</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol type=\"a\"><li>Form: subject + might + bare infinitive (verb without 'to')</li><li>Meaning: \u201cmight\u201d is used for making a suggestion or recommendation. It's not as strong as \u201chad better\u201d. We commonly use the verb \u201chave\u201d with \u201cmight\u201d. </li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We believe this idea <span class=\"underline\">might</span> attract more people to our business.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The new clients <span class=\"underline\">ought</span> to be loyal to our company. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We'd <span class=\"underline\">better</span> pick a date for the event now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That is something that <span class=\"underline\">ought to</span> be discussed soon. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"underline\">might want</span> to include him in this conversation. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking Negative Questions ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When asking questions in English, we sometimes use negative questions. They have a different word order and can be contracted and uncontracted. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Contracted negative questions follow this form: auxiliary verb + n't + subject + verb ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Uncontracted negative questions are usually more formal and follow this form: auxiliary verb + not + subject + verb ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Negative questions are commonly used to ask for confirmation of something you believe is true or to ask for confirmation of a negative belief - the speaker is surprised in this case. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Shouldn't you be</span> writing this down?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Isn't this idea</span> just a new way of attracting more people to buy our products?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Wouldn't it be</span> better if we talked about this later? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Haven't we decided</span> on a date yet? ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to integrate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to combine two or more things into one", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Isn't the idea to integrate corporate social responsibility into this new business model?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in a conversation about corporate social responsibility.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "business model ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a representation of how different parts of a business will work together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This new business model has been approved by the board.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "do charity work ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to help people in need; to do something that will benefit society", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Research suggests current consumers respond better when companies do charity work. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ethical standards", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a measure or benchmark of what is morally right or wrong", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The company ought to comply with ethical standards and develop a sense of responsibility towards the community.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to develop a sense of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get an understanding or an idea of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I would like to develop a sense of community.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "launch ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the introduction of a new product to the public", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have prepared for the external launch.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8l